{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789799943,"nonce":"yOrUKxpCpaU2DqGfeSt+w5SDBa0=","title":"Tiered: a callee reached only from compiled code never left its first tier","message":"Calls were counted by the interpreter, and a loop asked for promotion\nafter 1024 header visits in one frame. A library function called from\ncompiled code (nqueens' place calling zb_set_sub, zb_set_find_hashed,\nzb_any_kind) was reached through its cell, counted nowhere, and kept its\nfirst-call baseline for the life of the process: the whole hot path ran\nat tier 0. The promotion path then compiled the module's body of a lazy\nfunction, which is the unoptimised one (e79b58b), and refused every\nfunction returning a list header (aggregate ABI).\n\nFix: tier-0 code counts its entries in a per-bead counter and asks for\npromotion at 2048 (OSR_REQUEST_CALLS); the first-call compile's\noptimised bodies are kept (TieredBackend::optimized_bodies) and every\nlater tier compiles those; the LLVM entry ABI admits a growable list\nheader returned by address as it does one passed by address, and a\nreturn that would hand back a copy is a codegen error. A panic inside\nan LLVM compile is caught and reported as a failed compile, since the\npromoter thread carries every later promotion. nqueens 8.1 s to 6.7 s,\nmeteor 100 ms to 80 ms.","files":null}]}